/*!
  \page example_cxx_customize_kdtree_page Customizing the nodes of a kd-tree

  This example defines a kd-tree whose inner nodes store their bounding box, by providing custom node types to
  Ponca::KdTreeDefaultTraits. The new attribute is filled when the nodes are configured during the construction of
  the tree, and read afterwards from the nodes of the tree.

  Build and run:
  \code{.sh}
  cmake --build build --target ponca_customize_kdtree
  ./build/examples/cpp/ponca_customize_kdtree
  \endcode

  See also \ref spatialpartitioning_kdtree_extending.

  \include cpp/ponca_customize_kdtree.cpp
*/
